# nautilus Development Guidelines

Last updated: 2026-04-09

## Active Technologies

- **Portal**: TypeScript, Next.js (App Router) in `frontend/`
- **API**: Python 3.11+, FastAPI in `backend/`
- **Data**: In-memory repository (dev) with PostgreSQL-ready shapes; `DATABASE_URL` reserved for Postgres + SQLAlchemy/asyncpg
- **Dev auth**: Header stub (`X-Dev-Tenant-Slug`, `X-Dev-User-Sub`) until OIDC is wired

## Project Structure

```text
frontend/
├── src/app/
├── src/components/
└── src/lib/api/

backend/
├── app/routers/
├── app/repositories/
└── tests/
```

## Commands

- Portal: `cd frontend && npm run dev` / `npm run lint`
- API: `cd backend && .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000` (or `python -m uvicorn` after `Activate.ps1`)
- API tests: `cd backend && .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest`

## Code Style

Tenant scope on every API read path; audit append-only for configured shareholder actions; avoid logging raw PII; constitution v1.1.0 polyglot boundaries documented in plans when UI and API split.

## Recent Changes

- main: Institutional portal UI; expanded `/api/*` (dashboard, securities, notices); `frontend/` path; constitution 1.1.0 polyglot + UX-inspiration rules

